 C/GL:,NAME,DTRAN  /01.06.84/    . Refill the input line from stdin
C===========================================================
C C/GL - stdin input-refill helper, called from C/GF and from
C  C/CO's reset path.  This is the only user of READ*, so it is
C  the stdin path only: it runs PASEOF (the MONCARD eof test)
C  then, if data is real, calls READ* to pull one console/card
C  line (<=80 chars) into the file's 14-word buffer at FILE[12].
C  (Disk files refill from the *70 syscall path instead, in
C  PASINBUF, not from here.)
C
C  Labelled READLINE in p_sys.asm.
C===========================================================
C Register convention (see FILE.md):
C   M12 = base of the FILE record being acted on
C   M1  = runtime constant table ([M1+8] = 1U, [M1+9] = integer-tag
C         mask, [M1+12] = positive-mantissa mask, [M1+25B] = MSB;
C         [M1+3..5] and [M1+35B..37B] are runtime scratch)
C   M13 = link register set by the calling VJM
C   M14 = secondary link (used inside packed-mode helpers)
 PASEOFCD:,LC,1              . end-of-file sentinel record
 PASEOF:,SUBP,               . MONCARD eof-card detector
 READ*:,SUBP,                . read one stdin line into a 14-word buffer
 C/CB:,SUBP,                 . close the current buffer window
 C/RACPAK:,SUBP,             . unpack one element from the buffer
 C/RS:,SUBP,                 . return through the stack top
 ,ITA,13
 1,XTS,10B                   . push link, ACC := [M1+8]
 12,ATX,10B                  . stash f^ in FILE[8]
 13,VJM,PASEOF               . check end-of-input card
 ,UZA,ATEOF                  . EOF -> common tail
 ,ITA,8
 ,ITS,12                     . push M8, M12
 15,ATX,
 12,XTS,14B                  . push FILE[12] (buf start)
 13,VJM,READ*                . read one stdin line (<=80 chars) into the buffer
 ,NTR,3
 15,XTA,
 ,STI,12                     . restore M12
 ,ATI,8                      . restore M8
 12,WTC,14B
 ,XTA,
 ,UTC,PASEOFCD               . C := address of EOF sentinel for following AEX
 ,AEX,
 ,U1A,CLOSEBUF
 ATEOF:1,XTA,10B             . on EOF: reset f^
 12,ATX,2                    . FILE[2] := f^
 12,ATX,30B                  . FILE[24]:= f^
 CLOSEBUF:14,VJM,C/CB        . flush the buffer window
 13,VTM,C/RS
 ,UJ,C/RACPAK                . unpack via C/RACPAK
 ,END,
